 "interpretation": "This assumption is load-bearing, more so than expected. A matched %fT>MIC target of 40% leaves 60% of each interval BELOW the MIC, so the filament window is open for much of the matched-exposure comparison too, not only in failing arms. Giving meropenem the full ceftazidime coefficient narrows the matched-exposure cost ratio by up to 35% at the nominal yield, and collapses the 0.5x MIC ratio from about 35 to about 1.1. The ORDERING survives every fraction tested and the matched-exposure ratio stays several-fold, so no conclusion reverses; but the claim that the kill-independent pathway is PBP-3-exclusive is doing real work in the reported magnitudes, and the evidence for exclusivity is weak. The sub-MIC regime is where this is decided.",
 "not_done": "Meropenem's filament coefficient is not estimated and no default is changed. Doing so needs an experiment measuring release and viable counts together across sub-inhibitory exposures for both agents, which is prediction 1 of the manuscript extended below the MIC.",
